  "subject": "a woman whose boyfriend's model railway slowly takes over their dining table track by track, until they eat dinner on the sofa and the little train delivers the soy sauce",
  "caption": "Mandarin bluegrass, traditional string-band style. Rapid three-finger banjo rolls, flatpicked acoustic guitar runs, sawing fiddle double-stops, mandolin chop on the backbeat, slapped upright bass. Live room sound, no drums, natural acoustic. Female alto lead with close male harmony on choruses, bright and conversational. 132 BPM, G major. Cheerful, rollicking and teasing. No drum kit, no electric guitar, no pop synths, no autotune, no country-pop polish.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - banjo roll, fiddle kickoff]\n\n[Verse 1]\n你說只放一小段\n鐵軌就從盤子旁邊過\n第二週多了一座橋\n第三週多了車站\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我的碗被擠到邊邊\n你說那是月台\n\n[Chorus]\n餐桌上的火車 嘟嘟嘟\n繞過醬油繞過湯\n我們搬到沙發吃飯\n你還在幫它鋪軌\n\n[Verse 2]\n晚上我喊一聲醬油\n小火車慢慢開過來\n車廂載著一小瓶\n停在我的手邊\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n你戴著列車長的帽子\n說請注意月台間隙\n\n[Chorus]\n餐桌上的火車 嘟嘟嘟\n這班專門送醬油\n沙發其實也不錯\n只要火車準時來\n\n[Outro - banjo and fiddle trade licks]",
